    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0470" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/995.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Czaykowski
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Cape Haitien</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Zamor Government fallen in the north. Zamor with troops embarked on board Haitian
                    warship for Gonaives. President Zamor believed to be at or going to Gonaives.
                    Revolutionists in Cape. <hi rendition="#italic">Tacoma’s</hi> forces landed and
                    control foreign district.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Czaykowski</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
